                <pb facs="0616" n="492" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg492"/>

                <head>No. 297.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hunter to Mr. Everett</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-10-20"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 20,
                        1881</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 268.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Acknowledging the receipt of your dispatch,
                    No. 254, of the 27th ultimo, in relation to the invitation to the von Steuben
                    family to attend the Yorktown centennial celebration, I have to inform you that
                    your action in securing passage on the Herder, at the expense of this
                    government, for the seven officers who accepted the invitation in question, is
                    fully approved by this Department.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>W. HUNTER,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                        Secretary</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
